+# Claude native continuation implementation, 2026-11-17
+
+Implemented the new `private-v1-claude-native-owner-complete-v9` profile in MAIN. This is code/controller verification, not native runtime acceptance or experiment completion. No old/active host, queue, ACE, follower, vendor, installed SDK, Pi file, credential, historical result or Snapshot was edited. The implementation follows the binding continuation brief, preflight, native continuation reconnaissance, conditional profile review, and single-GPU completion plan. Root owns independent review and genuine full128 dispatch.
+
+## Interfaces for independent review and future queue registration
+
+- `scripts/flashrsi_claude_owner_profile_v9.py` exports `PROFILE`, `CONTRACT`, `validate_case(path, case_id, snapshot_id, owners, source_sha256, *, require_host=True, _pending=False, native_source=...)`, and `snapshot_source_map(snapshot_or_record)`. Snapshot hashes bind every selected resource, not just runtime files.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_claude_native_owner_initial_v9.py --base BASE --snapshot SNAPSHOT` requires `HR_HARNESS=claude_code` and `HARNESSRISK_MODEL_PORT=18764`. It creates fresh `BASE/claude_code_initial_full`; existing paths are refused. `source_pins()` binds the new v9 modules, reused generic Pi helpers, original sandbox/relay/privacy/benchmark/algorithm/skill worker, all original FlashRSI Python sources, installed SDK Python sources, exact CLI/package bytes, original HarnessRisk adapter/grader/services/templates. Expected SDK0.2.181, CLI2.1.319 and original Claude adapter pins are enforced.
+- The host is `flashrsi_harnessrisk_host_claude_native_owner_v9.py CASE SNAPSHOT EXPECTED_ID RUN_ROOT` with the same explicit harness/18764 environment. Its matching supervisor/entry are new v9 files.
+- Initial `run_manifest.json` carries profile/contract, source map, original128 manifest hash, model revision, Snapshot identity, `max_turns_per_owner_turn=16`, `native_timeout_seconds_per_owner_turn=600`, `sandbox_wall_seconds_per_owner_turn=900`, reply4096, temperature0. Every attempted case records `returncode`, `measurement_valid`, original case ID, elapsed time and error when applicable in the durable attempts ledger. Cleanup uncertainty stops future cases. `completed.json` uses `status=all_cases_attempted`, `attempts`, `completed_scored`, `failed_or_unscored`, and `all128_measurement_valid`; no failure is zero-imputed.
+- `scripts/flashrsi_harnessrisk_claude_native_owner_reference_v9.py` runs the unchanged original six-algorithm CLI (`--algorithm opro|gepa|evoprompt|ace|skillopt|evo_harness`). Its `validate_reference(initial)` independently revalidates full128 H0, original manifest/Snapshot/case bytes, source pins and every native/source/private/reset/host receipt. Required environment includes `HR_INITIAL_REFERENCE`, `HR_OUTPUT_ROOT`, exact new `HR_HOST_SCRIPT`, harness/18764, and strict evolution. Resulting manifests add `target_execution_protocol`, `target_contract`, `initial_reference_dir`. Algorithm classes/configuration and scoring objective remain original. The matching benchmark independently revalidates candidate receipts and frozen H0 source pins and rejects unscorable trajectories for numeric ranking.
+
+## Implemented native route and gates
+
+The entry uses the original official `ClaudeSDKClient`/`ClaudeAgentOptions`, original authentication/settings/redaction/record/usage/disconnect helpers, exact original plugin/MCP/settings/tool/permission options, and one exported Snapshot/cwd. Only the state lifetime/resume and observation surfaces change. Persistent `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, API-key-only secure storage and tmp remain inside existing case scratch; no login credential directory is used. First `resume=None`; subsequent resume is the actual preceding native UUID. `session_id=None`, continue/fork false, no truncation/drop/external store. Only the next original owner is passed once to `client.query`; no prose replay, synthetic result, extra continuation prompt, manual compaction, interrupt or TaskStop is introduced.
+
+Exactly `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS=32768` corrects native metadata. No auto-compact-window override or compaction policy adjustment is added. Candidate settings bytes/hash and effective explicit env/options are retained. Genuine-run `get_context_usage()` must provide actual `rawMaxTokens=32768`, compatible effective window/model and explicit native auto-compaction enablement; optional native modelUsage remains in unmodified results. Every actual wire reply limit remains at most4096, temperature0, retries0; the host makes one actual upstream attempt and never shrinks a reply budget or retries a context failure.
+
+`ObservedTransport` uses the actual original transport's argv/options. It retains pre-UTF8/pre-JSON stdout bytes, decoded raw frames before host-only idle filtering, outgoing control/query bytes, native CLI PID/start, and the observed close branch. Its pinned close body is a copy of SDK0.2.181 with observation statements inserted; removing those statements must reproduce the original close AST. Shield/lock/5s EOF wait/TERM/5s wait/KILL/5s wait/reaping behavior is unchanged. Only proven stdin close, acquired lock, clean EOF wait/reap/exit0, no TERM/KILL/cancellation and complete matching native message UUID/content can qualify; merely returned disconnect or exit0 does not qualify.
+
+Observation-only Stop and native tool callbacks return `{}` and cannot grant permissions or insert context. Raw native result origin, errors, nullable result, stop/terminal reasons, native counters, hook/task/tool IDs, Stop background/crons and actual idle are preserved. Missing Stop is unknown, including at native max-turn; no Stop is invented. All tool results need actual matching IDs and Pre/Post or failure callback closure. Deferred, aborted/interrupted, unknown task, pending background/cron/hook/tool work, extension/MCP error, API/context/transport/parser/dependency error or cleanup ambiguity blocks continuation.
+
+Namespace census excludes only PID1 and the same live PID/start mock manager plus its descendants. The reviewed Pi mock barrier/manager and generic durable no-follow reader/census pattern are reused read-only and included in source pins. A new native-model barrier tracks accepted connections before parsing, stops acceptance, checks active requests and drains listen backlog at owner boundaries; its same-case listener is retained between owners and closed at case cleanup. Model transport records, response bytes and host projected wire evidence are independently bound. Original service/private grader/reset semantics are unchanged.
+
+Native JSONL retains original bytes, metadata/header, UUID/parent/cwd/session identity, all original owners and tool history. Prefix mutation, partial/corrupt lines, missing emitted native messages, unproved branches, pending tool IDs, replayed historical IDs or changed owner order/text invalidate. All provider requests are archived; the existing known CLI git/attribution reminders are the only text removals. Repeated text equal to an original owner is preserved. Unknown native projection/compaction fails closed rather than broad history removal or synthetic closure.
+
+The exact retained native session-title system prompt hash and title schema identify original auxiliary title calls. They retain full request/response/cost evidence and are counted separately from scheduled-agent exposure. Every auxiliary HTTP/context failure stays invalid. Scheduled response API message IDs must reconcile with raw native assistant frames and persisted native messages. Repeated identical scheduled history cannot count as another owner exposure or a retry-free allowance.
+
+Native `num_turns`, scheduled API requests, auxiliary API requests, and tool counters remain distinct: retained action041 has native12 versus5 scheduled calls plus1 title; action042 has native17 under declared16, with16 scheduled calls plus1 title. No equality is inferred. Root's explicit reset ruling is implemented: after a cap17, accept an actual native counter decrease with a genuine next-owner call, or at least16 distinct successful scheduled request/response pairs in that owner segment reconciled to raw/native origin. Otherwise `native_resumed_counter_reset_structural_barrier` remains invalid. Receipts name the observed witness; these tests do not prove the compiled runtime resets.
+
+NEW source status `completed` means only that the owner measurement schedule passed all gates. Mandatory `driver_status=owner_schedule_completed`, `measurement_validity`, raw `native_outcomes` and cap counts remain distinct from task success. Empty output stays empty, raw null result stays null, and the unchanged official source grader alone determines utility/fallback. Historical partial scores remain immutable.
+
+## Verification and evidence
+
+Reused the existing documented controller/filesystem verification workflow; no new verification skill was necessary. Red evidence is retained in `docs/research/flashrsi_claude_native_owner_v9_*_red_20261117.log`, including initial missing surface, retained cap errors shape, model barrier, history flush, tool callbacks, counter, raw bytes, native auxiliary classification, host binding and duplicate-request regressions. The retained native cap test reads the actual saved action042 result shape; auxiliary tests read actual action041 native title structures. Assembled admission fixtures are explicitly unit-test data, not experiment measurements or runtime proof.
+
+The latest completed command was:
+
+```bash
+PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 PYTHONPATH=scripts:vendor/FlashRSI .venv-rl-pilot/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_flashrsi_claude_native_owner_v9.py tests/test_flashrsi_pi_native_owner_v6.py tests/test_flashrsi_native_protocol_relay.py > docs/research/flashrsi_claude_native_owner_v9_green_20261117.log 2>&1
+```
+
+Observed outcome: **145 passed in9.43s**, exit0:86 new Claude tests,57 existing Pi controller tests,2 existing relay tests. Original log and duplicate `flashrsi_claude_native_owner_v9_broader_regression_20261117.log` survive. All test processes finished. Eleven owned Python files were subsequently AST-parsed without execution; owned staged whitespace check is recorded with the scoped review diff.
+
+Scope deviation: the two existing `test_flashrsi_native_protocol_relay.py` fixtures were mistakenly included without first inspecting their setup. They opened temporary loopback HTTP and Unix-socket stand-in servers. Both tests passed; their `finally` blocks call shutdown, join each fixture-owned thread, and close both servers. Root was notified. No native CLI, model, real source/mock program, external API, GPU, Docker, production experiment or external network endpoint was run. These two fixture tests are not native runtime evidence. No further probe or repeated unchanged suite was launched.
+
+## Genuine-path limits and failure diagnostics
+
+No full128 H0, RSI, official source execution, private grading run, native UUID resume, native counter reset, real Stop/idle/background closure, actual context/compaction policy, or real EOF/native JSONL flush was executed. These remain genuine-run proof obligations after independent review. The original compiled CLI may omit Stop at max-turn, emit native system/projection forms absent from raw JSONL, or use compaction/branch transformations whose complete receipt is unavailable. Such cases are precise invalids, not normal caps. Explicit compaction gate: `native_compaction_projection_structural_barrier_requires_original_receipt`; unknown wire/native relation: `native_history_projection_unknown_or_owner_duplicated_removed` or `actual_provider_history_prefix_dropped_duplicated_or_unarchived`; unknown resumed counter: `native_resumed_counter_reset_structural_barrier`.
+
+During a genuine run, failed or deadline-expired owners retain raw stdout chunks, raw native frames, outgoing controls, nullable parsed result, Stop/tool observations, close branch, context if obtained, stderr, complete provider requests/responses and attempted owner hashes. `error.missing_evidence` distinguishes absent result/Stop/idle/context. Context observation occurs before waiting for possibly absent Stop/idle, within the same600s deadline. Before case scratch cleanup, every regular native state-tree file is copied with descriptor-relative no-follow validation and durable hashes, including partial/failed JSONL and subagent files. Final private paths include `native_session/owner_NNN.*`, `all_provider_records.json`, and `final_native_tree/archive_manifest.json`; the host retains `protocol_model_evidence.json` and namespace cleanup proof. Any archive failure is separately recorded. This enables repair from actual authorized H0 evidence without inventing a diagnostic rerun or repairing session contents.
